From b3aa31113de2a931a2d08159cc3782e217c2bcba Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: piano-fedora <dev@piano.invalid>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 04:10:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] linux: carry the GPI DMA deep-idle fix into the 7.3 series

The NT36532E touch controller is read over GENI SPI in GPI DMA mode. On
SM8750 the system low power domain is entered while the DMA runs and
stalls it, so 5450-byte reads take 2.46 ms or 4.85 ms instead of
2.0-2.7 ms. The stalled transactions are the host-side cause of a
whole-screen washout on the TDDI panel while the touch firmware scans.

yzddmr6/linux-sm8750-piano 322fd1bfbda9 fixes this by holding a 2000 us
CPU latency limit from prepare_message to unprepare_message in GPI mode
only. It is rebased onto the 7.3 tree here: the only difference from
upstream is hunk context, which this tree shifts by the extra
struct geni_spi_desc block above spi_geni_master. The code is otherwise
byte-identical.

series.json and config/release.json move their target_tree together.
